16 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a mango leaf disease classification system, starting with input images of damaged leaves, followed by data augmentation, training using a proposed deep learning model and several pretrained models, evaluation via accuracy metrics, and final prediction with visual explanations using GradCAM and LIME.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Flowchart showing a deep learning model pipeline for leaf image classification, including steps for image preprocessing, data augmentation, a DenseNet with channel attention modules, five-fold cross-validation, soft voting ensemble for final prediction, and visualization with GradCAM and LIME.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Confusion matrix and ROC curve for an ensemble model on the MLDID dataset show high classification accuracy and ROC AUC near one for all classes. Ten line charts display training and validation loss and accuracy curves for five folds of MangoLeafNet, each indicating low loss and high, stable accuracy for both training and validation sets over epochs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Composite figure showing a confusion matrix and multi-class ROC curve for an ensemble model detecting mango leaf diseases, alongside ten line charts depicting training and validation loss and accuracy across five folds, demonstrating high model performance and stability.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Composite figure with: top left, a confusion matrix showing strong correct predictions for Anthracnose, Black Sooty Mold, and Healthy classes; top right, a multi-class ROC curve with area under the curve values near one for all classes; below, ten line graphs displaying training and validation loss and accuracy over epochs for five cross-validation folds of MangoLeafNet, with all curves converging toward low loss and high accuracy.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Three rows show paired images of mango leaves with Grad-CAM visualizations. Each row presents an original leaf image on the left and a Grad-CAM heatmap overlay on the right, highlighting areas important for disease classification across different datasets and conditions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Figure with three panels, each showing leaf disease classification and LIME explanation. Panel A: anthracnose-infected leaf and highlighted regions supporting prediction. Panel B: mango leaf with bacterial canker and LIME regions in red and green. Panel C: leaf with black sooty mold and highlighted explanation segments.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
